1317: #  ------------------------------------------------------------ #505 sgirergbroundtrip
1318: #  horrible_getputpixel()'s RGB GET read buf[1..3] while its RGB PUT writes the three channels at
1319: #  buf[0..2] and an explicit pad at buf[3] -- so an RGB pixel did not survive its own round trip and
1320: #  the red channel was dropped.  RGB was the ONLY 32-bit colour mode in the file failing this way.
1321: #
1322: #  THE ARM WAS CHOSEN ON EVIDENCE FROM A DIFFERENT DEVICE, which is what makes the warrant
1323: #  non-circular: dev_sgi_gbe.c's scanout reads the same tile memory back as
1324: #  (buf[0]<<24)+(buf[1]<<16)+(buf[2]<<8)+buf[3], and CRMFB_MODE_TYP_RGB8 takes R,G,B from bits
1325: #  31..24 / 23..16 / 15..8 -- byte 0 is R and byte 3 is UNUSED.  The pad sits at buf[3] because the
1326: #  CONSUMER ignores buf[3], not because PUT writes a zero there.
1327: #
1328: #  `rgb depth64' IS NOT DECORATION -- IT CLOSES A MEASURED CLAUSE-(d) FLOOR BREACH.  The first kill
1329: #  table's M6_cond (guard kept, repair conditioned on `bufdepth == 4') scored a CLEAN SWEEP 6/6,
1330: #  because every session then used BUFDEPTH_32 and the mutant's fix branch was the only one the
1331: #  detector ever executed.  Its mirror M7_cond8 (exempting bufdepth 8 instead) also dies, so the
1332: #  WIDTH AXIS is closed rather than the one cell the mutant happened to use.
