**C’s arithmetic is substantially correct; its records history is not independently evidenced.**

For the implementation:

> `width = msb - lsb + 1`  
> `uint32_t mask = (1 << width) - 1;`

I enumerated the field pairs arithmetically, without executing the shifts. Under the stated 32-bit-`int` interpretation:

| Set | Count |
|---|---:|
| All `msb`, `lsb` pairs | **1,024** |
| Negative width | **465** |
| Zero width | **31** |
| Width 31 | **2** |
| Width 32 | **1** |
| Unsafe mask expression | **468** |
| `msb < lsb` | **496** |
| Intersection of the preceding two sets | **465** |
| Union | **499** |

Thus **468**, **31**, **496** and **465** are correct in their respective roles. **499** is the union count, not the unsafe-expression count. `1 << 0` is defined. [Expression](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_arm_instr.c:1454)

